# Naming conventions

Canonical docs: `docs/NAMING_CONVENTIONS.md` + `docs/DECISION_DEFAULTS.md`.

## Cheat sheet

- API / DB / DTO fields: `snake_case`
- Frontend locals/functions: `camelCase`; types/components: `PascalCase`
- Backend Python locals: `snake_case`; classes: `PascalCase`
- Tables: plural `snake_case`
- New enum wire values: lowercase `snake_case`
- Indexes: `ix_…`; unique: `uq_…`

## Forbidden in new code

- camelCase API/DTO fields
- camelCase `serialization_alias`
- Expanding dual-read (`lesson_id || lessonId`) or scattered mappers
- Inventing synonyms already covered by `DECISION_DEFAULTS.md` (e.g. `creator_id` vs `created_by`)
- Mass-renaming legacy code in unrelated PRs
